From 3ee47ebb01a6d75991fea964175f7f9f89f06563 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AERA | Erez Yaary <yaary@me.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:09:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] common/tools/mkhelp.py: the family's help generator
 (guidelines 4.3)

From EPlay's tools/mkhelp.py (EPDF's, EContact's, EMail's and
EHypView's before it), so that every app makes its guide with one
generator: docs/GUIDE.md into NAME.STG, a page a "## " section, tables
in columns, every line within 75 columns, links between sections, the
Atari character set, the same file each time.

What was EPlay's own is now an option: --app (the name in the page
titles; the guide's first heading's first word by default),
--database (the guide's first heading), --subject (Programs) and
--help-page (Keyboard; none with ""). NAME.HYP is the output's name.
EPlay's guide comes out byte for byte as before with
--database "EPlay - music on the Falcon" --subject Sound.

tests/help/test_mkhelp.py: pages, links, tables, listings, pictures
left out, @ as @@, the widths, CR/LF, the character set, the same file
twice, the options, then helpfront.py page over it and hcp compiling
the two (when there is one): all pass, with hcp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SZeNoDozTmbWt4s2sFN9eL
